Template: dlp-lab/configure
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Configure and start DLP file protection now?
 Select the local desktop user and Telegram executable in the next questions.
 File and session monitoring are system services. The standard deployment
 command is sudo dlp-setup connection.json.

Template: dlp-lab/user
Type: string
Description: Local desktop username to protect:
 Enter the existing non-root login name of the user who runs Telegram.
 An empty value leaves protection unconfigured.

Template: dlp-lab/telegram
Type: string
Default: /usr/bin/telegram-desktop
Description: Absolute path to the Telegram executable:
 The executable and its parent directories must be administrator-owned and
 protected against modification by ordinary users. AppImage files in a user's
 home directory are not supported by this system installation.
